@startuml state-assigned-personnel
' Title: SM-04 Assigned personnel (AP) status (PlantUML version of state-assigned-personnel.mmd, keep both in sync)
' Source: enums/AssignedPersonnelStatus.java, service/AreaAssignedPersonnelService.java (create, revoke, revokeAllOfUser,
'   computeStatus), service/AreaService.java (revokeAssignedPersonnelOnDeactivation), service/UserService.java · Generated from main @ e474968
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam roundCorner 6
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam nodesep 65
skinparam ranksep 45
skinparam stateStartColor #000000
skinparam stateEndColor #000000
skinparam stateBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam stateBorderColor #475569
skinparam stateFontColor #0F172A
skinparam stateArrowColor #2563EB
hide empty description

title SM-04 Assigned Personnel Status

state UPCOMING : computed
state ACTIVE : computed
state EXPIRED : computed
state REVOKED : stored as revoked_at

[*] --> UPCOMING : Facility Manager assigns user\n[validFrom > now, no overlap]
[*] --> ACTIVE : Facility Manager assigns user\n[validFrom = now, at most 5 min in the past (ERR_AP_013)]

UPCOMING --> ACTIVE : Time passes\n[now >= validFrom]
ACTIVE --> EXPIRED : Time passes\n[validTo set and now >= validTo]

UPCOMING --> REVOKED : Facility Manager revokes [reason]
ACTIVE --> REVOKED : Facility Manager revokes [reason]
UPCOMING --> REVOKED : Administrator deactivates or deletes\nthe user (BR-AP-24, BR-AP-25),\nor deactivates the area (BR-AD-04)
ACTIVE --> REVOKED : Administrator deactivates or deletes\nthe user (BR-AP-24, BR-AP-25),\nor deactivates the area (BR-AD-04)

REVOKED --> [*]
EXPIRED --> [*]

note right of EXPIRED
  One record per grant: validity cannot be edited.
  To grant again, create a new record
  (it may start exactly at the previous validTo).
  Revoking an EXPIRED record -> 409 ERR_AP_012.
end note

note left of REVOKED
  Status is NOT stored. computeStatus(ap, now):
  revoked_at set -> REVOKED
  now < valid_from -> UPCOMING
  valid_to set and now >= valid_to -> EXPIRED
  otherwise ACTIVE
end note
@enduml
